{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>Is it such.</b> A day for a man to afflict his soul — duplicated, for it is the fast:" "<b>To bow.</b> Hiphil of the doubled [root] in the pattern of לקב אויבי (Numbers 23:11):" "<b>Like a reed.</b> A soft plant that bends its head; it is well known:" "<b>Spread.</b> The dagesh in the tzadi is because of the missing yod of the root, like אצרך (Jeremiah 1:5); the full form is ייציע, and the meaning is to set out a bedding [cf.] ושק ואפר יציע (Esther 4:3):"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 58, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:00:07.955364101Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}